  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nHello,\r\nWhen I was work about 1-2 months ago and testing synapse homeserver version 1.63, I created directory `/sync` in nginx. I am using homeserver with nginx reverse proxy on localhost port `8008`. The Synapse domain is `https://chat.xxx.com` also in that time was working with https://github.com/Awesome-Technologies/synapse-admin and add / deactive users.\r\nI have set `/sync` in nginx chat config file to load data from `/var/www/html/chat/sync/` . When I have touched it in browser, https://chat.xxx.com/sync, all database flushed!\r\n\r\nDatabase was using SQLite.\r\n\r\nI think if `/sync` directory is sensitive, you should note it on config documents.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n-\r\n\r\n### Homeserver\r\n\r\nsynapse\r\n\r\n### Synapse Version\r\n\r\n1.63\r\n\r\n### Installation Method\r\n\r\nDebian packages from packages.matrix.org\r\n\r\n### Platform\r\n\r\nDebian 11 - VMware Esxi\r\n\r\n### Relevant log output\r\n\r\n```shell\r\n-\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\r\n\r\n_No response_",
